<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<suite name="mam_newnuc_coag" version="1.0">
  <!--
    Bundled validation suite for MAM new-particle nucleation + coagulation.

    Validates the ported modal_aero_newnuc_run and modal_aero_coag_run
    chained, against the CAM aerochem snapshot tapes
    (chem_aero_snapshot_test_design.md), method B: bit-true vmr states are
    read straight from the capture fields via the registry, so any
    difference at a check target is a real port bug.

    Two verdicts per run (ncdata = ncdata_check = the "after" tape):
      input   : the working mam_vmr initializes from aerochem_vmr (the P_end
                capture = CAM's newnuc entry), so no inject scheme is needed.
                newnuc's del-h2so4 inputs (mam_del_h2so4_gasprod/_aeruptk)
                and met fields (state_zm, pbuf_pblh, pbuf_CLD, Q) are read
                from the same tape.
      newnuc  : modal_aero_newnuc_ccpp applies the nucleation tendency to
                the working vmr; mam_vmr_checkpoint_postnewnuc stages it in
                mam_vmr_postnewnuc, compared against aerochem_vmr_postnewnuc
                (P2 capture) = VERDICT 1.
      coag    : modal_aero_coag_ccpp consumes newnuc's computed output
                (bit-true P2 iff newnuc is b4b) and mutates the working vmr
                IN PLACE; mam_vmr_checkpoint_postcoag stages it in
                mam_vmr_postcoag, compared against aerochem_vmr_postcoag
                (P3 capture) = VERDICT 2.

    Failure isolation: postnewnuc dirty means the newnuc port; postnewnuc
    clean but postcoag dirty means the coag entry state / chaining (coag
    itself is b4b certified standalone, suite_mam_coag).

    EXPECTED NOISE in the check report: the working mam_vmr is compared
    against aerochem_vmr (P_end) but holds the post-coag state by design;
    only the two checkpoint comparisons are the b4b verdicts.

    Init-time ordering:
      mam_constituents / sulfur_chemistry_stub - register the constituents so
                the snapshot fields resolve to indices (H2SO4 must exist for
                the portable gasaerexch init's validation)
      mam_mode_metadata     - mode geometry + index maps; sets loffset=0
      mam_gasaerexch_setup  - runs the portable gasaerexch init, whose public
                protected pcage state the COAG init phase consumes (newnuc
                has no such dependency)
      to_be_ccppized_temporary - wv_sat_init, for the qsat call inside
                modal_aero_newnuc_run
      modal_aero_newnuc_ccpp / modal_aero_coag_ccpp (init phases) - index and
                pair-table resolution, calling the portable inits

    No unpack/apply here: both schemes work purely in vmr space and the
    constituent tendency for the cluster is recovered by the difference-based
    mam_vmr_unpack only in the assembled suite.
  -->

  <group name="physics_before_coupler">
    <!-- Register MAM aerosol species + condensable gases as CCPP constituents -->
    <scheme>mam_constituents</scheme>
    <scheme>sulfur_chemistry_stub</scheme>

    <!-- Init-only: mode metadata + species index maps (also provides loffset=0) -->
    <scheme>mam_mode_metadata</scheme>

    <!-- Init-only: portable gasaerexch init stores the pcage aging state that
         the coag init phase reads; must precede modal_aero_coag_ccpp -->
    <scheme>mam_gasaerexch_setup</scheme>

    <!-- Init-only: wv_sat_init (newnuc computes relative humidity via qsat) -->
    <scheme>to_be_ccppized_temporary</scheme>

    <!-- New-particle nucleation: tendency-return, applied to the working vmr
         by the wrapper -->
    <scheme>modal_aero_newnuc_ccpp</scheme><!-- dropsonde:portable=modal_aero_newnuc_run -->

    <!-- VERDICT 1: stage the post-newnuc state for the ncdata_check
         comparison against aerochem_vmr_postnewnuc -->
    <scheme>mam_vmr_checkpoint_postnewnuc</scheme>

    <!-- Coagulation: init phase builds the pair tables and calls the portable
         modal_aero_coag_init; run phase mutates the working vmr in place -->
    <scheme>modal_aero_coag_ccpp</scheme><!-- dropsonde:portable=modal_aero_coag_run -->

    <!-- VERDICT 2: stage the post-coag state for the ncdata_check comparison
         against aerochem_vmr_postcoag -->
    <scheme>mam_vmr_checkpoint_postcoag</scheme>
  </group>
</suite>
